{"slug":"/students/subjects/mathematics/foundations/ratios-proportions-rates/","source":"students/subjects/mathematics/foundations/ratios-proportions-rates.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Ratios, Proportions & Rates | Mathematics","description":"","subject":"mathematics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/mathematics/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations</a></nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -divide text-green-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Ratios, Proportions &amp; Rates\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding proportional relationships, unit rates, and scaling problems in mathematics.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Understand the concept of ratio and how to simplify it</li>\n          <li>• Solve problems involving direct and inverse proportion</li>\n          <li>• Calculate and apply unit rates to real-world problems</li>\n          <li>• Use proportional reasoning to solve scaling problems</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Understanding Ratios -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Understanding Ratios\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A <strong class=\"text-green-600\">ratio</strong> compares two or more quantities of the same kind. It shows how many times one quantity is contained in another.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Writing Ratios:</p>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li><strong>Using colon:</strong> 3:4 (read as \"3 to 4\")</li>\n              <li><strong>Using fraction:</strong> 3/4</li>\n              <li><strong>Using words:</strong> \"3 to 4\" or \"3 is to 4\"</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 1 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example 1: Simplifying Ratios</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Simplify the ratio 24:36</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of 24 and 36</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">GCD(24, 36) = 12</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Divide both numbers by the GCD</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">24 ÷ 12 : 36 ÷ 12 = 2 : 3</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: 2:3</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Proportions -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Proportions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A <strong class=\"text-green-600\">proportion</strong> is a statement that two ratios are equal. When two quantities are in proportion, changing one affects the other in a predictable way.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n              <p class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Direct Proportion</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-blue-700\">As one quantity increases, the other increases at the same rate.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-blue-600 mt-2 italic\">Example: More items = more cost</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n              <p class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Inverse Proportion</p>\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-purple-700\">As one quantity increases, the other decreases.</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-purple-600 mt-2 italic\">Example: More workers = less time to complete a task</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 2 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example 2: Direct Proportion</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">If 5 apples cost ₦300, how much will 8 apples cost?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the cost per apple (unit rate)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">₦300 ÷ 5 = ₦60 per apple</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Multiply by the required quantity</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">8 × ₦60 = ₦480</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Alternative Method (Proportion):</strong></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono mt-1\">5 : 8 = 300 : x</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 font-mono\">x = (8 × 300) ÷ 5 = ₦480</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: ₦480</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 3 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example 3: Inverse Proportion</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">If 6 workers can complete a job in 10 days, how long will it take 15 workers?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Calculate total work (worker-days)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">6 workers × 10 days = 60 worker-days</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Divide by new number of workers</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">60 ÷ 15 = 4 days</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-purple-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: 4 days</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm mt-1\">More workers = less time (inverse relationship)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Rates -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Rates and Unit Rates\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A <strong class=\"text-green-600\">rate</strong> compares two quantities with different units. A <strong class=\"text-green-600\">unit rate</strong> is a rate per one unit.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mt-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Common Examples of Rates:</p>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• <strong>Speed:</strong> km/h, m/s (distance per time)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Unit price:</strong> ₦/kg, $/item (cost per quantity)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Productivity:</strong> items/hour (output per time)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>Heart rate:</strong> beats/minute</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example 4 -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example 4: Rate Problems</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">A car travels 180 km in 3 hours. How far will it travel in 5 hours at the same speed?</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Find the rate (speed)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">Speed = 180 km ÷ 3 h = 60 km/h</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Apply the rate to find distance</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">Distance = 60 km/h × 5 h = 300 km</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: 300 km</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Practice Problems -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-blue-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Simplify the ratio 45:75</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>GCD(45, 75) = 15</p>\n                <p>45 ÷ 15 : 75 ÷ 15 = <strong>3:5</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. If 3 pencils cost ₦120, find the cost of 7 pencils.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Unit cost = ₦120 ÷ 3 = ₦40 per pencil</p>\n                <p>Cost of 7 = 7 × ₦40 = <strong>₦280</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. A car uses 15 litres of fuel to travel 225 km. How far can it travel on 20 litres?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Rate = 225 km ÷ 15 L = 15 km/L</p>\n                <p>Distance = 15 km/L × 20 L = <strong>300 km</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. 4 men can paint a house in 6 days. How many days will 8 men take?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Total work = 4 × 6 = 24 man-days</p>\n                <p>Days with 8 men = 24 ÷ 8 = <strong>3 days</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">5. Share ₦500 between A and B in the ratio 3:2</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Total parts = 3 + 2 = 5</p>\n                <p>Value of one part = ₦500 ÷ 5 = ₦100</p>\n                <p>A gets: 3 × ₦100 = <strong>₦300</strong></p>\n                <p>B gets: 2 × ₦100 = <strong>₦200</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-teal-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• A ratio compares quantities of the same kind; always simplify to lowest terms</li>\n          <li>• In direct proportion, both quantities increase together</li>\n          <li>• In inverse proportion, one quantity increases as the other decreases</li>\n          <li>• A unit rate is always expressed per ONE unit (e.g., km per 1 hour)</li>\n          <li>• Cross-multiplication is useful for solving proportion problems</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-green-50 to-teal-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);} \n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .step-card{transition:all 0.2s ease;}\n    .step-card:hover{transform:translateX(4px);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}